This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   The user asked me to build the complete cinema seat-booking web application described in `spec/README.md`, as the React application already scaffolded in this Nx workspace (Nx project `cinescope` in `apps/cinescope`). The stack is described in `spec/stack.md`. Work is split into 7 tickets in `spec/tickets/` (01-movie-list, 02-auditorium-map, 03-seat-selection, 04-booking-summary, 05-checkout, 06-confirmation, 07-final-pass) which must be implemented **in order**. `spec/README.md` is stated to be the complete specification — I must not ask any clarifying questions, and must choose the simplest option wherever the spec is silent. The task is finished **only when every ticket is done and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds**. Key environment rules from the spec: package manager is pnpm (not npm/yarn); app served at port 4200 (must not change); no new dependencies may be added (everything needed is already installed — MUI 9, MUI X Date Pickers, dayjs, react-router-dom 6); `db.json` must not be edited by hand; desktop-only viewport (1280×720+), all text in English; UI library (MUI) components must be used for every button, text field, checkbox, toast, and the datepicker — the seat map/legend/selected-seats panel are hand-drawn by the app itself.

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Nx 23 monorepo with inferred Vite build/serve/test targets (via `@nx/vite` and `@nx/vitest` plugins in nx.json) and ESLint (`@nx/eslint` plugin) — `project.json` targets block is empty (`{}`), targets are inferred.
   - React 19 + React Router 6 (`BrowserRouter`), Vite 8, Vitest 4, MUI 9 (`@mui/material`, `@mui/icons-material`), MUI X Date Pickers 9.14 with dayjs adapter (`AdapterDayjs`), SCSS.
   - `sessionStorage`-backed booking state machine shared via React Context (`BookingContext`), representing an in-progress booking (screeningId, selected seat identifiers, checkout form values, paid flag, customer email) that persists across reloads but is scoped per-screening.
   - Seat identifier scheme `R<row>C<column>` (e.g., `R7C12`); couches occupy two adjacent column identifiers (e.g., `R15C5` + `R15C6`) and are toggled/priced/counted as a single atomic unit worth 2 seats.
   - Auditorium geometry: 15 rows × 24 columns, two 2-seat-wide aisles (between columns 4/5 and 20/21), an "entrance" gap (not an aisle) replacing columns 1–4 in rows 1–10, accessible seats at row 1 columns 10–15, all of row 15 rendered as 12 couches (column pairs 1-2, 3-4, …, 23-24).
   - Strict `data-testid` / data-attribute contract (section 9 of the spec) that must be matched exactly — this drives nearly every component's markup.
   - MUI v9's narrower/stricter typing: `Stack` no longer accepts `alignItems`/`justifyContent`/`flexWrap` as direct props without `component`, requiring these to go through `sx` instead; `TextField`/`DatePicker` use a new `slotProps` API (replacing legacy `InputProps`/`InputLabelProps`) whose nested slot prop types (e.g., `inputLabel`, `formHelperText`, DatePicker's internal `PickersTextField` slots) are strict component-prop interfaces that reject arbitrary `data-testid` keys unless the slot's prop type explicitly supports `WithDataAttributes`.
   - Backend: `json-server` 0.17.4 serving `db.json` at `http://localhost:3000`, with `/movies`, `/movies/:id`, `/screenings`, `/screenings?date=`, `/screenings?movieId=`, `/screenings/:id`, and `POST /reservations`.
   - Budget-conscious tool usage: discovered that batching multiple `Write`/`Edit` tool calls into a single assistant turn (parallel tool calls) was dramatically cheaper than issuing them sequentially one-per-turn, given the small ($5) USD budget for this session — this materially changed my approach to writing files (batched 5–6 files per message).
   - Sandbox networking quirk: within the Bash tool's Node process, `fetch`/`http.get` to `http://localhost:3000` or `http://127.0.0.1:3000` failed with `ECONNREFUSED`/`fetch failed`, even though the `json-server` process was confirmed running and listening; only `http://[::1]:3000` (explicit IPv6 loopback) succeeded. This appears to be a Bash-tool-specific network restriction on IPv4 loopback, not expected to reflect the real browser/grading environment, so I deprioritized further live end-to-end testing via this route.

3. Files and Code Sections:
   - **`/workspace/project/spec/README.md`, `/workspace/project/spec/stack.md`, `/workspace/project/spec/tickets/*.md`** — Read in full; these are the complete specification and ticket breakdown driving all implementation decisions (not modified).
   - **`/workspace/project/db.json`** — Read (not modified); contains 5 movies, 26 screenings (dates 2026-09-15 through 2026-09-21), empty reservations array. Confirmed must never be hand-edited.
   - **`/workspace/project/package.json`** — Read; confirmed dependencies already present (no new deps needed), pnpm package manager, `pnpm api` script runs `json-server --watch db.json --port 3000`.
   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/main.tsx`** — Read only; already wraps `<App />` with `ThemeProvider`, `CssBaseline`, `LocalizationProvider` (AdapterDayjs), and `BrowserRouter`. Not modified — kept as the top-level composition root.
   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/app.tsx`** — Rewritten from a stub (`<Routes />`) to:
     ```tsx
     import { Navigate, Route, Routes } from 'react-router-dom';
     import { BookingProvider } from './booking/BookingContext';
     import { ToastProvider } from './components/Toast';
     import MovieList from './routes/MovieList';
     import SeatSelection from './routes/SeatSelection';
     import Summary from './routes/Summary';
     import Checkout from './routes/Checkout';
     import Confirmation from './routes/Confirmation';

     export function App() {
       return (
         <ToastProvider>
           <BookingProvider>
             <Routes>
               <Route path="/" element={<MovieList />} />
               <Route path="/screenings/:id/seats" element={<SeatSelection />} />
               <Route path="/screenings/:id/summary" element={<Summary />} />
               <Route path="/screenings/:id/checkout" element={<Checkout />} />
               <Route path="/confirmation" element={<Confirmation />} />
               <Route path="*" element={<Navigate to="/" replace />} />
             </Routes>
           </BookingProvider>
         </ToastProvider>
       );
     }
     export default App;
     ```
     This satisfies the five routes (section 3) and the catch-all redirect to `/`.
   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/app.spec.tsx`** — Modified (original test only wrapped `<App />` in `BrowserRouter`, which broke once `DayPicker`'s MUI `DatePicker` required a `LocalizationProvider` context — threw "MUI X: Can not find the date and time pickers localization context"). Fixed by adding the `LocalizationProvider`/`AdapterDayjs` wrapper around `BrowserRouter`:
     ```tsx
     import { render } from '@testing-library/react';
     import { BrowserRouter } from 'react-router-dom';
     import { LocalizationProvider } from '@mui/x-date-pickers/LocalizationProvider';
     import { AdapterDayjs } from '@mui/x-date-pickers/AdapterDayjs';
     import App from './app';

     describe('App', () => {
       it('should render successfully', () => {
         const { baseElement } = render(
           <LocalizationProvider dateAdapter={AdapterDayjs}>
             <BrowserRouter>
               <App />
             </BrowserRouter>
           </LocalizationProvider>,
         );
         expect(baseElement).toBeTruthy();
       });
     });
     ```
     Test now passes, but during the last test run it logged a stderr warning: `React does not recognize the \`htmlInput\` prop on a DOM element` — see Errors section below; this is unresolved.
   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/api/types.ts`** (new) — `Movie`, `Screening`, `Customer`, `Reservation` interfaces matching spec section 2.1 exactly, plus `CreateReservationPayload = Omit<Reservation, 'id'>`.
   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/api/client.ts`** (new) — `BASE_URL = 'http://localhost:3000'`; generic `getJSON<T>(path)` helper throwing on non-OK responses; exports `fetchMovies`, `fetchMovie(id)`, `fetchScreeningsByDate(date)`, `fetchScreening(id)`, `createReservation(payload)` (POST with `Content-Type: application/json`, throws on non-OK).
   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/utils/dates.ts`** (new) — `ISO_DATE_FORMAT = 'YYYY-MM-DD'`; `todayISO()`; `isValidISODate(value)` (regex + dayjs round-trip check); `resolveSelectedDate(param)` (missing/invalid/past → today, via string comparison since ISO format sorts correctly); `nextDays(startDateISO, count)`; `weekdayFull(dateISO)` (`dddd` format); `formatShowDate(dateISO, time)` → e.g. `"Tuesday 15 Sep 16:00"` using `dayjs(\`${dateISO}T${time}\`)` then `${d.format('dddd')} ${d.date()} ${d.format('MMM')} ${time}`.
   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/utils/seats.ts`** (new) — Core domain logic:
     - Constants: `ROW_COUNT=15`, `COLUMN_COUNT=24`, `COUCH_ROW=15`, `COUCH_PRICE=89`, `MAX_SEATS=10`.
     - `SeatState = 'available' | 'selected' | 'unavailable' | 'accessible'`.
     - `seatId(row, column)`, `parseSeatId(id)` (regex `/^R(\d+)C(\d+)$/`).
     - `isAccessibleSeat(row, column)` → `row === 1 && column >= 10 && column <= 15`.
     - `priceForRow(row)` → 25 (rows ≤5), 32 (rows ≤10), 39 (rows 11-14).
     - `formatPrice(amount)` → `${amount.toFixed(2)} PLN`.
     - `STATE_COLORS` record mapping each `SeatState` to its hex color (`#2E7D32`, `#F9A825`, `#C62828`, `#1565C0`).
     - `RowCell` union (`SeatCell | CouchCell | AisleCell | GapCell`) and `buildRowCells(row)` — generates the ordered list of cells for a row: entrance gap (rows ≤10) or seat block 1–4 (rows 11-15), aisle, seat/couch block 5–20, aisle, seat/couch block 21–24; couch rows pair columns two at a time.
     - `SeatItem` interface and `deriveSeatItems(seatIds)` — groups a flat seat-id array into row-sorted, column-sorted `SeatItem`s (seat or couch), each with `ids`, `price`, `seatLabel` (e.g. `"12"` or `"3-4"`).
     - `formatSelectedSeatsLines(seatIds)` — produces `{row, text}` lines like `"Row 7: 11, 12"` / `"Row 15: 1-2"` for the selected-seats panel, using `deriveSeatItems` internally.
   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/booking/BookingContext.tsx`** (new) — `BookingFormValues` (firstName, lastName, email, confirmEmail, phone, termsAccepted), `BookingState` (screeningId, seats, form, paid, customerEmail), `STORAGE_KEY = 'cinescope-booking'`, `readStoredBooking()`/`emptyBooking(screeningId)` helpers, `BookingProvider` (lazy-inits state from `sessionStorage`, persists via `useEffect` on every change, removes key when booking becomes `null`), exposing: `ensureBookingForScreening(screeningId)` (keeps existing booking if same screeningId and unpaid, else starts fresh), `toggleSeats(ids)` (atomic add/remove respecting the 10-seat cap, returns boolean success), `removeSeats(ids)`, `setFormField(field, value)` (generic over `keyof BookingFormValues`), `markPaid(email)`, `clearBooking()`. `useBooking()` hook throws if used outside provider.
   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/components/Toast.tsx`** (new, then fixed) — `ToastProvider`/`useToast` using MUI `Snackbar` + `Alert` (`data-testid="toast"`), single-toast-at-a-time via `setTimeout`-based 4s auto-dismiss, new toast resets the timer. Fixed TS error: `useRef<ReturnType<typeof setTimeout>>()` (no initial value) → `useRef<ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | undefined>(undefined)`.
   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/components/DayPicker.tsx`** (new, then fixed, **still has an unresolved runtime bug**) — Renders `data-testid="day-picker"` container, 5 `data-testid="day-button"` buttons (`Today` + 4 weekday names) with `data-date`/`data-selected`, and a MUI `DatePicker` with `minDate={dayjs(today)}` and `data-testid="date-picker"` intended on the underlying native input. Current (problematic) code:
     ```tsx
     <DatePicker
       value={dayjs(selectedDate)}
       minDate={dayjs(today)}
       onChange={(value: Dayjs | null) => {
         if (value && value.isValid()) {
           onSelect(value.format('YYYY-MM-DD'));
         }
       }}
       slotProps={{ textField: { htmlInput: { 'data-testid': 'date-picker' } } } as never}
     />
     ```
     This passed typecheck via the `as never` cast but produces a runtime React warning (`React does not recognize the \`htmlInput\` prop on a DOM element`), meaning the cast is bypassing type safety but the prop is NOT being correctly routed to the native `<input>` — it appears to be literally spread as an `htmlInput` attribute onto some DOM element instead of being interpreted as the nested slot prop. **This is unresolved and is the most important pending fix.**
     Earlier failed attempts for this line (chronological): `slotProps={{ textField: { inputProps: { 'data-testid': 'date-picker' } } }}` (TS error: `inputProps` doesn't exist on `PickersTextFieldProps`), then `slotProps={{ textField: { htmlInput: { 'data-testid': 'date-picker' } } }}` (TS error: `htmlInput` doesn't exist on `SlotComponentPropsFromProps<PickersTextFieldProps,...>` — i.e., DatePicker's own `textField` slot prop type, which is NOT the same as `PickersTextFieldProps`'s own internal `slotProps.htmlInput`), then cast to `DatePickerProps['slotProps']` (abandoned due to complexity), then finally cast to `as never` (passes typecheck, but is runtime-broken per the warning).
     **Key new finding just before this summary was triggered**: grepping `PickersTextField.types.d.mts` revealed:
     ```
     interface PickersTextFieldSlots { ... htmlInput?: React.ElementType; ... }
     export interface PickersTextFieldSlotProps<InputPropsType extends PickersInputBaseProps> {
       ...
       htmlInput?: WithDataAttributes<React.ComponentPropsWithRef<'input'>>;
     }
     export interface PickersTextFieldSlotsAndSlotProps<InputPropsType extends PickersInputBaseProps> {
       ...
       slots?: PickersTextFieldSlots;
       ...
       slotProps?: PickersTextFieldSlotProps<InputPropsType>;
     }
     ```
     This strongly suggests the correct path requires one more level of nesting: the `DatePicker`'s `slotProps.textField` object should itself contain a nested `slotProps.htmlInput` (since `PickersTextField` — the component rendered by the `textField` slot — has its own `slots`/`slotProps` sub-API), i.e. something like:
     ```tsx
     slotProps={{ textField: { slotProps: { htmlInput: { 'data-testid': 'date-picker' } } } } }
     ```
     This was the exact line of investigation in progress when cut off — **not yet applied or verified**.
   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/routes/MovieList.tsx`** (new, then fixed) — Day picker + movie list screen per spec section 4: `Status` type (`'loading'|'error'|'loaded'`), `load()` callback fetching movies + date-filtered screenings in parallel, renders `movies-loading`, `movies-error` (+ `movies-retry-button`), `movies-empty`, or `movie-list` containing `movie-card`s (each with `movie-title`, `movie-genre`, `movie-runtime`, `movie-format`, and one `screening-button` per screening sorted by time). Fixed: `<Stack direction="row" spacing={1} flexWrap="wrap" sx={{ mt: 1 }}>` → `<Stack direction="row" spacing={1} sx={{ mt: 1, flexWrap: 'wrap' }}>` (MUI v9 Stack typing fix).
   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/routes/SeatSelection.tsx`** (new, then fixed multiple times) — The largest component: loads screening+movie (redirects to `/` on failure), calls `ensureBookingForScreening`, renders `seat-map-title`, `seat-map-subtitle` (via `formatShowDate`), `seat-limit-info`, `screen-indicator`, `seat-map` (rows via `buildRowCells`, each row = `seat-row` with `row-label-left`/`row-label-right`, `aisle`, `seat` (with `data-row`/`data-column`/`data-state`), or `couch` (with `data-row`/`data-column-start`/`data-column-end`/`data-state`)), `legend` (4 `legend-item`s), `selected-seats` panel (`selected-seats-count` + `selected-seats-row` lines via `formatSelectedSeatsLines`), and `cancel-button`/`continue-button`. Seat/couch click handlers call `toggleSeats` from `BookingContext` and show the `Maximum 10 seats per booking` toast on failure. Fixed three separate MUI `Stack` typing errors (legend container `justifyContent`, legend-item `alignItems`, action-buttons row `justifyContent`) by moving them into `sx`.
   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/routes/Summary.tsx`** (new, then fixed) — Loads screening+movie (redirects to `/` on failure), runs an on-mount-only booking-validity guard effect (`useEffect(() => {...}, [])` with an eslint-disable comment, since the check should only run on route entry, not on every booking change — important because removing seats updates `booking` and would otherwise incorrectly trigger a redirect to `/` instead of the spec's "removing the last item opens `/screenings/:id/seats`" behavior), renders `summary-title`, `summary-list` of `summary-item`s (`summary-item-title`, `summary-item-datetime`, `summary-item-row`, `summary-item-seat` — `Couch <a>-<b>` or plain column number, `summary-item-price`, `summary-item-remove-button`), `summary-total`, `back-button`, `confirm-button`. `handleRemove` navigates to the seat map when removing the last item. Fixed: moved `alignItems` into `sx` for the item `Stack`; removed an unused `eslint-disable-next-line react-hooks/exhaustive-deps` comment on the screening/movie-loading effect (its deps array `[screeningId]` was already correct, so the disable was flagged as an "Unused eslint-disable directive" lint warning).
   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/routes/Checkout.tsx`** (new, then fixed) — Validation functions (`firstNameError`, `lastNameError`, `emailError` using `EMAIL_REGEX = /^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/`, `confirmEmailError`, `phoneError` using `/^\d{9}$/`, `termsError`); local `touched` state (not persisted, per spec 7.1); `handlePay` marks all fields touched + shows `The form contains errors` toast on invalid submit, else POSTs via `createReservation` with seats reordered via `deriveSeatItems(...).flatMap(item => item.ids)` ("summary order"), `markPaid(form.email)` + navigate to `/confirmation` on success, or shows `Payment failed. Please try again.` toast on failure (form/values preserved). Renders `checkout-title`, 5 `TextField`s (first/last name, email, confirm email, phone) each with `slotProps.htmlInput` (data-testid for the input — did NOT need a cast, typechecked cleanly), `slotProps.inputLabel` and `slotProps.formHelperText` (both needed `as never` casts to satisfy TS — **same unresolved runtime-correctness concern as the DatePicker fix above, not yet verified**), a `FormGroup`/`FormControlLabel`/`Checkbox` for terms (`slotProps={{ input: { 'data-testid': 'terms-checkbox' } as never }}`, plus a manual `<span data-testid="terms-label">` and conditional `FormHelperText data-testid="terms-error"`), and `checkout-back-button`/`pay-button` (reading `Pay <total> PLN` or `Processing…` while submitting). On-mount-only guard effect same pattern as Summary.tsx. Final cast state after fixes (all 10 instances in this file now use `as never` instead of `as any`):
     ```tsx
     slotProps={{
       htmlInput: { 'data-testid': 'first-name-input' },
       inputLabel: { 'data-testid': 'first-name-label' } as never,
       formHelperText: { 'data-testid': 'first-name-error' } as never,
     }}
     ```
